# The build context is the repository root, because the kernel image needs both `kernel/` and
# `console/` in the relative positions the workspace expects (`askama.toml`). Everything that is
# not a build input is excluded — and key material and runtime state are excluded first, so that a
# stray seed cannot reach an image layer even by accident.

# --- never, under any circumstances ---
**/secrets/
**/keys/
*.seed
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/var/
deploy/genesis/
deploy/config/

# --- build artefacts ---
**/target/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/

# --- caches and tooling ---
.git/
.github/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.serena/
**/.DS_Store
*.log
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- not build inputs ---
docs/
spec/vectors/
